Building Spectre
================

Spectre is a privacy-focused node forked from Zcash. Build steps match the upstream Zcash toolchain.

## Requirements

- 64-bit Linux (recommended) or supported Unix/macOS
- ~6 GB RAM for linking; ~2 GB disk for proving params
- Dependencies: see `depends/` or `./zcutil/build.sh` (builds deps automatically on Linux)

## Quick build (Linux)

```bash
./zcutil/fetch-params.sh
./zcutil/build.sh -j$(nproc)
```

Binaries are written to `src/`:

- `spectred` — full node daemon
- `spectre-cli` — RPC client
- `spectre-tx` — transaction utility

## First run (regtest)

```bash
./src/spectred -regtest -daemon
./src/spectre-cli -regtest getblockchaininfo
```

Data directory: `~/.spectre/` (config file: `spectre.conf`).

